<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Venni</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Venni was fought near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the Sangam age, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> king Karikala defeated a coalition of the Chera and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> kings and eleven chieftains. Sangam poets celebrated it as a great victory that established Chola supremacy among the Tamil kingdoms. It is usually placed in the early centuries CE.</p></div>
